  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The parts are the same as in step 1. Nothing was added or dropped.",
   "The SEN136B5B has GND, 5V and SIG pins, matching the catalogue's ping-sensor type, so I used that type.",
   "The sensor's three legs go in neighbouring holes of one row: columns 9, 10 and 11, in the order GND, 5V, SIG. I used the half of the breadboard drawn at the top of the image, which is bank 'b' (rows f-j) in the catalogue's naming. The sensor is in row h and each jumper wire is in row g of the same column strip, so each wire shares a strip with its sensor pin.",
   "The exact column and row numbers are read off the image and are approximate. The wiring is as the tutorial states: 5V to the board's 5V pin, GND to the board's GND pin, SIG to digital pin 7.",
   "The Uno's GND pin next to pin 13 is taken as GND.1. The parts list gives 'hook-up wires' without a count. The image shows three: black for GND, orange for 5V and blue for SIG."
  ]
 },
